cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "WR-I is a preprint candidate. Cite the repository version until a publication DOI is assigned."
title: "Response-Defined World Spaces: Response Equivalence, Finite-Resolution Separation, and Identifiability of Global Realizations"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: "Malachevsky"
    given-names: "A. A."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-6009-3196"
version: "0.3-candidate"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AIDevelopersMonster/WREH"
url: "https://github.com/AIDevelopersMonster/WREH/tree/main/papers/WR-I"
abstract: >-
  WR-I develops the mathematical entry point of the World Realizability &
  Epistemic Horizons (WREH) programme. It studies admissible global
  realizations through families of observation protocols and their response
  maps, separating exact response equivalence, identifiability, protocol
  refinement, gauge redundancy, finite-resolution separation, and
  finite-tolerance indistinguishability.
keywords:
  - WREH
  - world realizability
  - response equivalence
  - identifiability
  - finite resolution
  - gauge redundancy
  - inverse problems
  - epistemic horizons
